section.service-page
  h1 Water Damage Restoration in Sydney
  p Burst flexi-hose, storm water, or a leak that's spread? drySafe provides water damage restoration across Sydney — fully self-serve, so you can book and pay online in minutes and get proper drying underway before the damage spreads any further.
  h2 What proper water damage restoration involves
  p Restoration is more than mopping up and pointing a fan at the wet patch. Done properly, it's a sequence:
  ul
    li #[strong Assessment:] mapping how far the water has travelled with moisture readings, and checking the water category to plan the job.
    li #[strong Extraction:] pulling the water out of carpet, underlay and hard floors before drying starts.
    li #[strong Proper drying:] air movers and dehumidifiers working together to draw moisture out of the structure, not just the surface.
    li #[strong Verified dry:] moisture meters confirm the home is back to its normal dry standard, documented for your records and your insurer.
  h2 Why it's worth doing properly
  p Water spreads into the parts of your home you can't see — underlay, subfloor, wall cavities, timber framing. A surface that feels dry can still be wet underneath, and that trapped moisture is what leads to warping, lifting, odour and lasting structural damage. Proper restoration targets the water you can't see and confirms it's gone, so a wet floor doesn't turn into a repair bill.
  h2 What drySafe handles
  ul
    li Emergency water extraction
    li Structural drying of carpet, underlay, subfloors and walls
    li Moisture monitoring and documented dry-down
    li Flooded and wet carpet drying
  h2 Serving Sydney
  p drySafe works across Greater Sydney, including City of Parramatta, Cumberland City, Ryde City and The Hills Shire. Local means drying equipment gets on site and running sooner — and the sooner it starts, the more of your home and belongings can be saved.
  h2 How it works — book online
  p drySafe is built to be self-serve. You check availability, book, and pay online — a few minutes, day or night — and that's the fastest way to get proper drying started.
  p If it's specifically a soaked carpet, see our guides to #[a(href='/blog/wet-carpet-drying-guide') wet carpet drying] and #[a(href='/blog/carpet-flood-damage') carpet flood damage]; for the full overview, see #[a(href='/blog/water-damage') water damage].
  h2 Ready when you are
  p If water's come through your Sydney home, don't wait it out — get proper drying underway before it spreads any further.
  a.btn-primary(href='https://drysafe.sydney') Book & pay online
